-- What the core 6th-level spells do, in a sentence or three of our own words. Shown
-- in place of the bare facts a spell's entry is built from (see Data/SpellSummaries.lua).
local _, ns = ...
local R = ns.Rules

R.SPELL_SUMMARIES = R.SPELL_SUMMARIES or {}
local S = R.SPELL_SUMMARIES

S["Arcane Gate"] = "Two linked portals open for up to 10 minutes, one within 10 feet of you and one up to 500 feet away. Anything that enters the open side of one steps out of the other. A bonus action turns the open sides around."
S["Blade Barrier"] = "A wall of spinning blades, up to 100 feet long or a ring 60 feet across, stands within 90 feet for up to 10 minutes. It gives three-quarters cover and is difficult terrain. A creature in it when it appears, or that enters or ends its turn there, takes 6d10 force damage, half on a successful Dexterity save."
S["Chain Lightning"] = "A bolt strikes a target within 150 feet and leaps to up to three more within 30 feet of it: each takes 10d8 lightning damage, half on a successful Dexterity save. One more leap for each slot level above 6th."
S["Circle of Death"] = "Deathly energy fills a 60-foot sphere within 150 feet: 8d8 necrotic damage, half on a successful Constitution save. 2d8 more for each slot level above 6th."
S["Conjure Fey"] = "A fey spirit appears within 60 feet for up to 10 minutes and you make a melee spell attack from it: 3d12 psychic damage plus your spellcasting modifier, and the target is frightened until the start of your next turn. A bonus action on later turns teleports it 30 feet and attacks again. 1d12 more for each slot level above 6th."
S["Contingency"] = "Takes 10 minutes. You cast a spell of 5th level or lower on yourself and hold it back: it takes effect the first time a trigger you describe happens within 10 days. Only one can be held at a time."
S["Create Undead"] = "Takes a minute, at night only. Up to three corpses of Small or Medium humanoids within 10 feet rise as ghouls that obey you for 24 hours; a bonus action commands those within 120 feet. Cast it again to keep control. Higher slots raise more, or stronger, undead."
S["Disintegrate"] = "A ray at a target within 60 feet: 10d6 + 40 force damage unless it passes a Dexterity save, and a creature reduced to 0 hit points turns to dust. It also destroys an object or a creation of magical force, Large or smaller. 3d6 more for each slot level above 6th."
S["Drawmij's Instant Summons"] = "Takes a minute. You mark an object of up to 10 pounds and tie it to a sapphire. Crushing the sapphire later brings the object to your hand from anywhere, or tells you who holds it and where."
S["Eyebite"] = "For up to a minute, when you cast it and with an action after, one creature within 60 feet must pass a Wisdom save or fall asleep, flee in panic or be sickened (poisoned), as you choose. A creature that has passed can't be targeted again."
S["Find the Path"] = "Takes a minute. For up to a day you know the distance and direction to a fixed place you are familiar with on your plane, and which way is most direct at every fork."
S["Flesh to Stone"] = "A creature within 60 feet that fails a Constitution save is restrained and saves again at the end of each of its turns: three successes end the spell, three failures turn it to stone. Hold your concentration for the full minute and it stays petrified. On the first success it only can't move for a turn."
S["Forbiddance"] = "Takes 10 minutes. For a day, up to 40,000 square feet you touch is closed to teleporting and planar travel. Creature types you pick among the otherworldly ones take 5d10 radiant or necrotic damage when they enter or end a turn there, unless they speak your password."
S["Globe of Invulnerability"] = "For up to a minute, spells of 5th level or lower cast from outside can't affect anything within 10 feet of where you stood. One level higher for each slot level above 6th."
S["Guards and Wards"] = "Takes an hour. For 24 hours a building of up to 2,500 square feet is defended: fog in the corridors, locked and hidden doors, webs on the stairs, and other tricks you place. Those you name, or who know the password, pass freely."
S["Harm"] = "A creature within 60 feet takes 14d6 necrotic damage, half on a successful Constitution save. If it fails, its hit point maximum drops by the damage taken."
S["Heal"] = "A creature within 60 feet regains 70 hit points and is no longer blinded, deafened or poisoned. 10 more for each slot level above 6th."
S["Heroes' Feast"] = "Takes a minute, then an hour to eat. Up to twelve creatures gain, for 24 hours, resistance to poison damage, immunity to being frightened or poisoned, and 2d10 extra hit points, both current and maximum."
S["Magic Jar"] = "Takes a minute. Your soul moves into a container and from there can try to take over a humanoid within 100 feet, which resists with a Charisma save. You keep your mind in its body. If the host dies you must pass a Charisma save to return to the jar; if the jar is destroyed while your body is out of reach, you die."
S["Mass Suggestion"] = "You give a reasonable-sounding course of action, in 25 words or fewer, to up to twelve creatures within 60 feet that understand you. Those that fail a Wisdom save are charmed and follow it for 24 hours, or until you or your allies harm them. Higher slots last 10, 30 and 366 days."
S["Move Earth"] = "For up to 2 hours you reshape dirt, sand or clay in an area up to 40 feet on a side within 120 feet: raise, lower, trench or wall it. Each change takes 10 minutes; stone and buildings are not shaped."
S["Otiluke's Freezing Sphere"] = "A globe of cold bursts in a 60-foot sphere within 300 feet: 10d6 cold damage, half on a successful Constitution save. It freezes the surface of water, trapping swimmers. You can also hold the globe to throw later. 1d6 more for each slot level above 6th."
S["Otto's Irresistible Dance"] = "A creature within 30 feet that fails a Wisdom save is charmed for up to a minute and dances on the spot: it has disadvantage on attacks and Dexterity saves, and attacks against it have advantage. It can spend its action to save again. On a success it still dances until the end of its next turn."
S["Planar Ally"] = "Takes 10 minutes. A power you know sends a celestial, elemental or fiend to a space within 60 feet. It is not bound to you: you bargain for its help, and it expects payment that fits the task."
S["Programmed Illusion"] = "An illusion of up to a 30-foot cube within 120 feet waits unseen until a trigger you set, then plays a scripted scene of up to 5 minutes with sound. It rests for 10 minutes and can trigger again, until dispelled."
S["Summon Fiend"] = "A fiendish spirit, a demon, devil or yugoloth, appears within 90 feet and fights for you for up to an hour, acting right after your turn on your spoken commands. A higher slot makes it stronger."
S["Sunbeam"] = "A beam in a line 60 feet long and 5 feet wide from you: 6d8 radiant damage and blinded until the start of your next turn; a successful Constitution save halves the damage and avoids the blindness. For up to a minute an action fires a new beam."
S["Tasha's Bubbling Cauldron"] = "A cauldron appears within 5 feet for 10 minutes, filled with a common or uncommon potion of your choice. You or an ally can draw one out as a bonus action, up to as many as your spellcasting modifier. Unused potions vanish when you cast it again."
S["Transport via Plants"] = "For a minute a Large or larger plant within 10 feet is linked to another plant you have seen or touched, anywhere on your plane. Stepping into one, for 5 feet of movement, brings a creature out of the other."
S["True Seeing"] = "For an hour a willing creature you touch has truesight out to 120 feet."
S["Wall of Ice"] = "A wall of ice of ten 10-foot panels, or a dome or globe up to 10 feet in radius, rises within 120 feet for up to 10 minutes. Creatures in its space when it appears take 10d6 cold damage, half on a successful Dexterity save. A broken section leaves freezing air: 5d6 cold damage to those passing through, half on a successful Constitution save. 2d6 and 1d6 more for each slot level above 6th."
S["Wall of Thorns"] = "A thorny wall up to 60 feet long, or a ring 20 feet across, rises within 120 feet for up to 10 minutes and blocks sight. Creatures in it when it appears take 7d8 piercing damage, half on a successful Dexterity save. Every foot moved through it costs 4, and entering it or ending a turn there deals 7d8 slashing, with the same save. 1d8 more to both for each slot level above 6th."
S["Wind Walk"] = "Takes a minute. You and up to ten willing creatures within 30 feet become wisps of cloud for 8 hours: flying at 300 feet and resisting bludgeoning, piercing and slashing damage, but able only to dash. Changing back, or into cloud again, takes a minute spent stunned."
S["Word of Recall"] = "You and up to five willing creatures within 5 feet teleport to a sanctuary you prepared earlier by casting this spell there."
